We report results in Fig. 7. We reach identification rates of 85.6 % for 20 % filtering (89.3 % for 10 % filtering, 93.2 % for 5 % filtering) using the CHNOPS batch, and identification rates 66.8% (70.6, 79.4 %) for the “contains FClBrI” batch with 20 % (10 and 5 %, respectively) filtering. Overall, SIRIUS 3 correctly identifies 81.1 % (84.8, 89.9 %) of the molecular formulas, 89.0 % (92.5, 94.7 %) are in the top 2, and 95.0 % (96.7, 98.2 %) are in the top 5, for 20 % (10, 5 %, respectively) filtering.Fig. 7
