By modeling the compound fragmentation as a tree, we make the implicit assumption that each fragment in the fragmentation spectrum is generated by a single fragmentation pathway. In practice, different fragmentation pathways may lead to fragments with identical molecular structure. The most prominent example is that two fragmentation events happen independently and in arbitrary order: we call this a “parallelogram” spanned by the losses a, b, and \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
